I have a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

---

# Member-ID refactor: full reference map

The target field `memberId` = `'<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>'` is a unification of three existing values, each currently produced by a distinct, well-separated class. All production logic lives in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/` plus the mapper, model, schema, and tests. Note one important stale-doc finding flagged at the end.

## 1. The domain model (persistent fields)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
```java
73	    @Column(name = "customer_code")
74	    private String customerCode;
75	
76	    @Column(name = "membership_number")
77	    private String membershipNumber;
...
189	    public String getCustomerCode() { return this.customerCode; }
193	    public void setCustomerCode(String customerCode) { this.customerCode = customerCode; }
197	    public String getMembershipNumber() { return this.membershipNumber; }
201	    public void setMembershipNumber(String membershipNumber) { this.membershipNumber = membershipNumber; }
```
There is **no** `checkDigit` field on the entity — it is derived at read time only (see mapper). `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, etc. are separate derived fields.

### DB columns (all four schema dialects)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/schema.sql:52-53` — `customer_code VARCHAR(20)`, `membership_number VARCHAR(32)`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql:45-46` — same
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/mysql/schema.sql:42-43` — same
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/postgres/schema.sql:40-41` — `customer_code TEXT`, `membership_number TEXT`

No `member_id`/`check_digit` columns exist anywhere.

## 2. customerCode — definition and computation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerCustomerCode.java` — the single source of truth. Format is **`<REGION>-<HASH8>`** (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D`).
```java
32	    public static final String UNKNOWN_REGION = "UNKNOWN";
34	    private static final char SEPARATOR = '-';
40	    public static String of(Owner owner) {
41	        return regionFor(owner) + SEPARATOR + hash8(OwnerTelephone.toE164OrRaw(owner.getTelephone())
42	                + owner.getLastName());
43	    }
49	    public static String regionFor(Owner owner) {
50	        String region = OwnerLocality.regionFor(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity());
51	        return region != null ? region : UNKNOWN_REGION;
52	    }
63	    public static String withSuffix(String base, int n) {
64	        return base + SEPARATOR + n;      // collision suffix: NSW-1A2B3C4D-2
65	    }
71	    public static String regionOf(String customerCode) {   // read-time region recovery
75	        int sep = customerCode.indexOf(SEPARATOR);
76	        return sep > 0 ? customerCode.substring(0, sep) : null;
77	    }
80	    private static String hash8(String value) {            // first 8 UPPER hex of SHA-256 (4 bytes)
82	        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(value.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
85	        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) { sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i])); }
```
Key points for the refactor:
- The `HASH8` you want is exactly this `hash8(toE164OrRaw(telephone) + lastName)` — **4 bytes, 8 UPPER-case hex chars**. (Note the SHA-256 identity you described, "normalizedTelephone + lastName first 8 hex", is this one — NOT the lower-case full-hex `OwnerIdentity.identityKey`, which is a different value; see §8.)
- `REGION` is already a prefix, no `-` inside it.
- The `'-'` separator is what couples region/hash halves and the collision suffix.

**Assignment step:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`
```java
22	    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
23	        owner.setCustomerCode(OwnerCustomerCode.of(owner));
24	    }
```
Its Javadoc (lines 13-16) already names the eventual unification: "the `membershipNumber` and its `checkDigit`, the create audit record and the read-time `locality` all read it."

## 3. Collision handling

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DeduplicateCustomerCode.java`
```java
26	    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
27	        String base = owner.getCustomerCode();
28	        Set<String> existing = new HashSet<>();
29	        for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) { existing.add(other.getCustomerCode()); }
32	        if (!existing.contains(base)) { return; }
35	        int n = 2;
36	        String candidate;
37	        do { candidate = OwnerCustomerCode.withSuffix(base, n); n++; }
41	        while (existing.contains(candidate));
42	        owner.setCustomerCode(candidate);
43	    }
```
Finds the smallest `n >= 2` producing a free `<base>-<n>`. Runs after assign, before membership number, inside the create transaction. Because `customerCode` can gain a `-<n>` suffix, any `memberId` built from it must decide whether `CHK`/collision suffix placement changes — the suffix currently lands at the end, before the check digit is computed.

## 4. membershipNumber — definition and computation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` — format **`<customerCode>-M<YY>`** (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M27`).
```java
19	    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
20	        String yy = FiscalYear.yy(owner.getRegistrationDate());
21	        owner.setMembershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + yy);
22	    }
```
So membershipNumber already embeds customerCode + the fiscal-year `YY`. Your target `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` splices these: REGION+HASH8 come from customerCode, FY from the `M<YY>`/fiscalYear label.

## 5. checkDigit — definition and computation (Luhn)

Derived at read time only, in the mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
```java
29	    @Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(checkDigit(owner))")
...
116	     * Computes the owner's check digit: a single Luhn check digit (0-9) over the digits contained
117	     * in {@code customerCode}, derived at read time. Returns {@code null} when no customer code...
120	    default Integer checkDigit(Owner owner) {
121	        String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
